<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Maurice, Duke of Saxe-Zeitz</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1619">1619</a>–1681</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Maurice was the first Duke of Saxe-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zeitz">Zeitz</a>, a younger son of Elector John George I of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxony">Saxony</a>. Under his father's will he received Zeitz in 1657 with the secularised bishopric of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/naumburg">Naumburg</a> and lands in the Vogtland, founding a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxons">Saxon</a> secundogeniture. He built the Moritzburg palace in Zeitz and kept a Lutheran court.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/maurice-duke-of-saxe-zeitz.jpg" alt="Maurice, Duke of Saxe-Zeitz" width="320" height="441" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Gabriel Tzschimmer · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Durchlauchtigste_Zusammenkunft_0019.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
